  "tip01Text": "Drinking water before a meal can help you feel fuller and reduce calorie intake.",
  "tip01Title": "Hydration",
  "tip02Text": "Lack of sleep can affect your weight. Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep per night.",
  "tip02Title": "Sleep",
  "tip03Text": "Weigh yourself at the same time every day, preferably in the morning after using the bathroom.",
  "tip03Title": "Routine",
  "tip04Text": "Weight fluctuates daily due to water retention. Focus on the weekly average rather than daily numbers.",
  "tip04Title": "Patience",
  "tip05Text": "Including a good source of protein in your meals helps maintain muscle mass and keeps you satiated.",
  "tip05Title": "Protein",
  "tip06Text": "High-fiber foods like vegetables and whole grains keep you full longer and aid digestion.",
  "tip06Title": "Fiber",
  "tip07Text": "Even 15 minutes of brisk walking daily can significantly improve your metabolic health.",
  "tip07Title": "Movement",
  "tip08Text": "Eat slowly and pay attention to your food. It takes about 20 minutes for your brain to realize you're full.",
  "tip08Title": "Mindful Eating",
  "tip09Text": "Consistency beats perfection. A minor slip-up won't ruin your progress if you get back on track.",
  "tip09Title": "Consistency",
  "tip10Text": "High sodium intake can cause water retention, leading to a temporary spike on the scale.",
  "tip10Title": "Sodium",
  "tip11Text": "If you feel hungry between meals, try drinking a glass of water first – thirst is often mistaken for hunger.",
  "tip11Title": "Snacks",
  "tip12Text": "Building muscle increases your resting metabolic rate, helping you burn more calories around the clock.",
  "tip12Title": "Resistance Training",
  "tip13Text": "High stress levels increase cortisol, which can lead to cravings and fat storage. Find time to unwind.",
  "tip13Title": "Stress",
  "tip14Text": "Aim to fill half your plate with vegetables to easily reduce calorie density and increase nutrient intake.",
  "tip14Title": "Vegetables",
  "tip15Text": "Hidden sugars in drinks and sauces add up quickly. Check labels to make informed choices.",
  "tip15Title": "Sugar",
  "tip16Text": "Using smaller plates can trick your brain into feeling satisfied with smaller portion sizes.",
  "tip16Title": "Portions",
  "tip17Text": "Rest and recovery are just as important as workouts. Muscles grow when they recover.",
  "tip17Title": "Rest Days",
  "tip18Text": "Calories from sodas, juices, and alcohol don't make you feel full. Stick mostly to water, tea, or coffee.",
  "tip18Title": "Liquid Calories",
  "tip19Text": "Preparing your meals in advance reduces the temptation to order takeout when you are tired.",
  "tip19Title": "Preparation",
  "tip20Text": "Tracking your food for even just a few days can help you discover hidden calories in your diet.",
  "tip20Title": "Journaling",
  "tip21Text": "Put your fork down between bites to naturally pace your eating and improve digestion.",
  "tip21Title": "Slow Down",
  "tip22Text": "Celebrate non-scale victories like clothes fitting better or having more energy during the day.",
  "tip22Title": "Celebrate",
  "tip23Text": "Keep your bedroom cool, dark, and quiet to improve sleep quality and support your metabolism.",
  "tip23Title": "Sleep Quality",
  "tip24Text": "Wait 10 minutes when a craving hits. Often, the urge will pass once you distract yourself.",
  "tip24Title": "Cravings",
  "tip25Text": "Keep healthy snacks visible on the counter and less healthy ones hidden away out of sight.",
  "tip25Title": "Environment",
  "tip26Text": "Don't slash your calories too drastically. A very low-calorie diet can slow down your metabolism.",
  "tip26Title": "Metabolism",
  "tip27Text": "Adding a short 10-minute walk after meals helps lower your blood sugar response.",
  "tip27Title": "Walking",
  "tip28Text": "Non-Exercise Activity Thermogenesis (NEAT) like fidgeting or taking the stairs burns more calories than you think.",
  "tip28Title": "NEAT",
  "tip29Text": "Your journey is unique. Avoid comparing your progress to others on social media.",
  "tip29Title": "Comparison",
  "tip30Text": "Be kind to yourself. A sustainable healthy lifestyle is built on self-care, not punishment.",
  "tip30Title": "Self-Compassion",
